Chapter: FwdTextSearchTest
  cites Foreword chapter TextSearch
  cites Foreword chapter StringUtils

 This printed "Foreword/TextSearch OK" and asserted nothing, which is how
 text-to-upper and text-to-lower sat here as no-ops without anybody
 noticing. Both were written against ASCII ranges (97..122, minus 32) in
 an encoding where lowercase is 13..38 and the offset is 26, so they
 returned every letter unchanged. A smoke test that only proves the
 chapter compiles cannot see a function that runs and does nothing.

Section: Entry
  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("upper: " & text-to-upper "hello")
    print-line-uni ("lower: " & text-to-lower "HELLO")
    print-line-uni ("mixed: " & text-to-upper "CodeX 42")
    print-line-uni ("contains: " & show (text-contains "hello world" "o w"))
    print-line-uni ("join: " & text-join "-" ["a", "b", "c"])
    print-line-uni ("pad-left: " & text-pad-left "7" 3 "0")
    print-line-uni ("pad-right: " & text-pad-right "7" 3 "0")
    print-line-uni "Foreword/TextSearch OK"
  end
